WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.151
The experiments span two very different domains.

00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:08.382
For continuous control, the authors use classic
MuJoCo locomotion tasks,

00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:12.613
with Walker2d as the primary testbed and Hopper,
HalfCheetah, Ant,

00:00:12.693 --> 00:00:16.844
and Humanoid for breadth.

00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:21.075
They clone from strong expert policies over a long
horizon of a thousand steps,

00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:25.305
and they deliberately set the dataset size so that
overfitting is not the issue.

00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:29.536
For language,

00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:33.767
they train two hundred and seventy million
parameter Transformers on TinyStories,

00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:37.998
a small synthetic dataset of simple children's
stories that keeps the setup tractable

00:00:38.078 --> 00:00:42.229
while still exhibiting the phenomenon.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:46.460
Reward is averaged over twenty initial conditions
so the oscillations are not just measurement noise.
